.TH NMEA 2
.SH NAME
nmea \- NMEA 0183 sentences as GPS fixes
.SH SYNOPSIS
.EX
include "nmea.m";
nmea := load Nmea Nmea->PATH;
Fix, Parser, Sat: import nmea;

init:      fn();
fields:    fn(s: string): (array of string, string);
timeof:    fn(s: string): string;

Parser.new:        fn(): ref Parser;
p.sentence:        fn(s: string): (list of ref Fix, string);
p.satellites:      fn(): string;
p.forget:          fn();
p.last:            ref Fix;

f.time:            fn(): string;
f.text:            fn(): string;
f.position:        fn(): string;
f.fixmode:         fn(): int;
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Nmea
reads the sentences a GPS receiver sends and assembles them into fixes.
.B Init
must be called first.
.PP
.B Fields
checks one sentence (a trailing newline and carriage return are
removed) and splits it at its commas, the address first:
.B $GPRMC,1,2*hh
gives
.BR "GPRMC 1 2" .
A sentence must begin with
.BR $ ;
its checksum, if it has one, must be right.
The error is
.BR "not a sentence" ,
.BR "checksum mismatch" ,
.BR "bad checksum field" ,
.BR "bad character" ,
.B "bad address field"
or
.BR "sentence too long" .
.PP
.B Timeof
gives the time a sentence carries, as
.IR hh : mm : ss ,
with a fraction if the receiver gives one, or nil.
.PP
A
.B Parser
takes a receiver's sentences in order.
.B Sentence
gives the fixes the sentence completed, oldest first, usually none or
one, or the error
.B fields
found.
RMC, GGA, GLL, GSA, GSV, GST, VTG and ZDA are read, from any
constellation's talker
.RB ( GP ,
.BR GL ,
.BR GA ,
.BR GB ,
.BR BD ,
.BR GQ ,
.BR GI ,
.BR GN );
others, and proprietary sentences, are taken and passed over.
A receiver sends a burst of sentences for each time it computes a
position, which ones and in what order varying by receiver.
A fix is complete when every kind of position sentence the receiver
has been seen to send (RMC, GGA, GLL) has arrived for one time, or a
sentence for a new time arrives first.
A fix with no position is given only when the last one had one, or
was the first.
.PP
.B P.last
is the last complete fix; sentences after it for the same time (a
GSA) are added to it.
.B Satellites
gives one line for each satellite in view: its system, PRN, elevation,
azimuth, signal to noise ratio, and 1 if it is in the fix, 0 if not,
with
.B -
for a value not known.
.B Forget
is for a new receiver: what the old one sent is forgotten, its last
fix kept.
.PP
A
.B Fix
holds what the receiver gave for one time.
Each value has a flag or a sentinel for unknown: the
.B has
flags, -1 for
.B sats
and
.BR mode ,
a negative value for a dilution or an error.
Latitude and longitude are degrees, north and east positive;
.B altitude
is metres above mean sea level;
.B speed
metres a second;
.B course
degrees true;
.B err
and
.B verr
metres, one sigma, from GST.
.B Time
is RFC 3339 if the date is known (from RMC or ZDA), nil if not.
.B Text
is the fix as one line of attr=value fields, those known only; see
.IR gpsfs (4).
.B Position
is
.RI ` "lat lon" '
to six places, or nil when there is no fix.
.B Fixmode
is
.BR Mnone ,
.B M2d
or
.BR M3d ,
the receiver's if it gave one.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/lib/nmea.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR gpsfs (4)
